====================================================================================================
{
 "id": "REQ-6-1",
 "name": "Protect Branches with Review and Status-Check Requirements",
 "type": "ATOMIC",
 "dependencies": [
  "REQ-4-3-1",
  "REQ-1-1-2"
 ],
 "description": "This feature builds on the persisted objects, opened pages, or authenticated-session context provided by REQ-4-3-1 (List and Switch Repository Branches) and REQ-1-1-2 (Sign In with an Existing Account); it must reuse that context and keep pages and data consistent after the context changes. A “branch protection rule” is a persistent merge restriction bound to one exact branch name, displayed in the frontend under Settings → Branches, with the backend storing the branch name and rule toggles. This product supports only two independently selectable requirements: “at least 1 valid Approve from someone other than the PR author” and “required check `test` is success”. For a given reviewer on the same current compare commit, only the reviewer's latest decision among Comment, Approve, and Request changes counts. The PR author cannot satisfy the approval requirement; any valid Request changes blocks merging; when the compare branch gains a new commit, all decisions become stale and a new review is required. “Checks” is the results area on the PR detail page attached to the current compare commit; the `test` status of pending, success, or failure, together with the setter and time, must be stored, and only a repository Admin may update that status from this area. The system blocks direct writes to a protected branch and applies the rule during subsequent PR merging. The repository provides a Settings link followed by a Branches link. The rule form opens from the Add branch protection rule button and contains a field labeled Branch name pattern (an exact branch name, with no wildcard semantics), checkboxes named Require 1 approval and Require status check test, and a Create button; an existing rule uses Save changes. After saving and reloading, the branch name is visible verbatim with the summaries 1 approval and Require status check test. For a non-Admin, Add branch protection rule is absent, even if Settings or Branches remain accessible; rejecting a save alone is insufficient. On the PR detail page, the Checks area is available on arrival, displays test: pending initially, and offers the Admin a combobox named test status with a clickable option named success and a Save button. Saving displays test: success and identifies the setter and time, and reloading preserves the result for that compare commit. Seed data comprises a repository Admin and a readable non-Admin account, a dedicated repository and exact branch name with no existing rule before creation, and a separate Open PR targeting protected main with its current test check initially pending.\n\nScreenshot reference:\n![image](reference/github-branch-protection.png)",
 "scenarios": [
  {
   "name": "REQ-6-1: Protect Branches with Review and Status-Check Requirements - Scenario 1",
   "steps": [
    {
     "keyword": "GIVEN",
     "content": "The visitor starts at the application home page in a fresh unauthenticated browser session. The seeded data is pull requests `Improve onboarding` and `Fix search`, branches `main` and `feature-search`, reviewer `bob-reviewer`, check `test`. A repository Admin is signed in and has opened “Settings” → “Branches”; the repository contains a `main` branch and an Open PR targeting `main`. Seed values: pull requests `Improve onboarding` and `Fix search`, branches `main` and `feature-search`, reviewer `bob-reviewer`, check `test`."
    },
    {
     "keyword": "WHEN",
     "content": "The Admin clicks “Add branch protection rule”, enters the exact branch name `main`, checks “Require 1 approval” and “Require status check test”, and clicks “Create” or “Save changes”; the Admin then updates `test` from pending to success in the PR's “Checks” area. Seed values: pull requests `Improve onboarding` and `Fix search`, branches `main` and `feature-search`, reviewer `bob-reviewer`, check `test`."
    },
    {
     "keyword": "THEN",
     "content": "The settings page displays exactly one rule for `main` with both requirements; the PR detail page persistently displays `test: success`, the setter, and time. A PR without 1 valid non-author approval, with any valid Request changes, or with `test` not equal to success is subsequently shown as unmergeable, and the protected branch cannot be directly updated to bypass the rule. Seed values: pull requests `Improve onboarding` and `Fix search`, branches `main` and `feature-search`, reviewer `bob-reviewer`, check `test`."
    },
    {
     "keyword": "THEN",
     "content": "After refreshing the settings page, the rule still exists; a non-Admin either does not see a savable rule-editing entry or has the request rejected with the rule unchanged. Seed values: pull requests `Improve onboarding` and `Fix search`, branches `main` and `feature-search`, reviewer `bob-reviewer`, check `test`."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "name": "REQ-6-1: Protect Branches with Review and Status-Check Requirements - Scenario 2",
   "steps": [
    {
     "keyword": "GIVEN",
     "content": "The visitor starts at the application home page in a fresh unauthenticated browser session. The seeded data is pull requests `Improve onboarding` and `Fix search`, branches `main` and `feature-search`, reviewer `bob-reviewer`, check `test`. A signed-in user without repository-administration permission opens the branch-protection settings page. Seed values: pull requests `Improve onboarding` and `Fix search`, branches `main` and `feature-search`, reviewer `bob-reviewer`, check `test`."
    },
    {
     "keyword": "WHEN",
     "content": "The user attempts to create or modify a branch protection rule. Seed values: pull requests `Improve onboarding` and `Fix search`, branches `main` and `feature-search`, reviewer `bob-reviewer`, check `test`."
    },
    {
     "keyword": "THEN",
     "content": "Branch-protection controls are unavailable to the non-administrator or the operation is rejected, and no protection rule is saved. Seed values: pull requests `Improve onboarding` and `Fix search`, branches `main` and `feature-search`, reviewer `bob-reviewer`, check `test`."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "name": "REQ-6-1: Protect Branches with Review and Status-Check Requirements - Scenario 3",
   "steps": [
    {
     "keyword": "GIVEN",
     "content": "The visitor starts at the application home page in a fresh unauthenticated browser session. The seeded data is pull requests `Improve onboarding` and `Fix search`, branches `main` and `feature-search`, reviewer `bob-reviewer`, check `test`. A repository Admin opens the detail page of an Open PR targeting protected `main`; the Checks area shows `test` as pending for the PR's current compare commit. Seed values: pull requests `Improve onboarding` and `Fix search`, branches `main` and `feature-search`, reviewer `bob-reviewer`, check `test`."
    },
    {
     "keyword": "WHEN",
     "content": "The Admin updates `test` to success in the Checks area and saves. Seed values: pull requests `Improve onboarding` and `Fix search`, branches `main` and `feature-search`, reviewer `bob-reviewer`, check `test`."
    },
    {
     "keyword": "THEN",
     "content": "The Checks area displays success, the setter, and the update time; after refreshing the PR detail page, that status still corresponds to the same compare commit. If the compare branch gains a new commit, the new compare commit starts with pending, and success from the old commit cannot be used for merging. Seed values: pull requests `Improve onboarding` and `Fix search`, branches `main` and `feature-search`, reviewer `bob-reviewer`, check `test`."
    }
   ]
  }
 ]
}
