{
 "id": "REQ-6-2-1",
 "name": "List and Filter Repository Pull Requests",
 "type": "ATOMIC",
 "dependencies": [
  "REQ-3-3"
 ],
 "description": "The Pull requests list page only reads PR records from the current repository; each row displays the number, title, author, status, source branch, and target branch. Any user with repository-view permission may filter by Draft/Open/Closed/Merged status, author, or review status; filtering only affects the current list display and does not modify PRs, branches, or reviews. The public list is directly accessible to a visitor and has an Open link for the status filter; selecting it displays the seeded Open PR as a link whose exact accessible name is its title. Opening that link displays the same title as a heading. After reloading the filtered list, that Open PR remains visible; leaving the page and reopening the list, then selecting Open again, shows the same PR. Seed data includes this public list and a stable, uniquely titled Open PR as well as the Closed PR and author used in the filtering scenario. This feature builds on the persisted objects, opened pages, or authenticated-session context provided by REQ-3-3 (View a Public Repository Overview); it must reuse that context and keep pages and data consistent after the context changes.\n\nScreenshot reference:\n![image](reference/github-pull-requests-list.png)",
 "scenarios": [
  {
   "name": "REQ-6-2-1: List and Filter Repository Pull Requests - Scenario 1",
   "steps": [
    {
     "keyword": "GIVEN",
     "content": "The visitor starts at the application home page in a fresh unauthenticated browser session. The seeded data is pull requests `Improve onboarding` and `Fix search`, branches `main` and `feature-search`, reviewer `bob-reviewer`, check `test`. The user has opened the “Pull requests” page of an accessible repository; the list contains one Open PR created by `alice` and one Closed PR created by `alice`. Seed values: pull requests `Improve onboarding` and `Fix search`, branches `main` and `feature-search`, reviewer `bob-reviewer`, check `test`."
    },
    {
     "keyword": "WHEN",
     "content": "The user selects “Open” and filters the author to `alice`. Seed values: pull requests `Improve onboarding` and `Fix search`, branches `main` and `feature-search`, reviewer `bob-reviewer`, check `test`."
    },
    {
     "keyword": "THEN",
     "content": "The list displays only the Open PR and shows its number, title, source/target branches, author, and status; clicking the title opens that PR's detail page. Seed values: pull requests `Improve onboarding` and `Fix search`, branches `main` and `feature-search`, reviewer `bob-reviewer`, check `test`."
    },
    {
     "keyword": "THEN",
     "content": "After switching to “Closed”, the Open PR is not displayed; filtering does not change the status or review data of any PR. Seed values: pull requests `Improve onboarding` and `Fix search`, branches `main` and `feature-search`, reviewer `bob-reviewer`, check `test`."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "name": "REQ-6-2-1: List and Filter Repository Pull Requests - Scenario 2",
   "steps": [
    {
     "keyword": "GIVEN",
     "content": "The visitor starts at the application home page in a fresh unauthenticated browser session. The seeded data is pull requests `Improve onboarding` and `Fix search`, branches `main` and `feature-search`, reviewer `bob-reviewer`, check `test`. The visitor starts at the application home page in a fresh unauthenticated browser session. Seed values: pull requests `Improve onboarding` and `Fix search`, branches `main` and `feature-search`, reviewer `bob-reviewer`, check `test`."
    },
    {
     "keyword": "WHEN",
     "content": "The user signs in as `alice-dev` with `Valid-password-123!` and follows the visible controls for the list and filter repository pull requests workflow. Seed values: pull requests `Improve onboarding` and `Fix search`, branches `main` and `feature-search`, reviewer `bob-reviewer`, check `test`."
    },
    {
     "keyword": "THEN",
     "content": "The page displays the required headings, controls, values, and status for the list and filter repository pull requests workflow. Seed values: pull requests `Improve onboarding` and `Fix search`, branches `main` and `feature-search`, reviewer `bob-reviewer`, check `test`."
    },
    {
     "keyword": "THEN",
     "content": "After refreshing or reopening the visible destination, the successful result remains persisted; a rejected action leaves the original state unchanged. Seed values: pull requests `Improve onboarding` and `Fix search`, branches `main` and `feature-search`, reviewer `bob-reviewer`, check `test`."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "name": "REQ-6-2-1: List and Filter Repository Pull Requests - Scenario 3",
   "steps": [
    {
     "keyword": "GIVEN",
     "content": "The visitor starts at the application home page in a fresh unauthenticated browser session. The seeded data is pull requests `Improve onboarding` and `Fix search`, branches `main` and `feature-search`, reviewer `bob-reviewer`, check `test`. The visitor starts at the application home page in a fresh unauthenticated browser session. Seed values: pull requests `Improve onboarding` and `Fix search`, branches `main` and `feature-search`, reviewer `bob-reviewer`, check `test`."
    },
    {
     "keyword": "WHEN",
     "content": "The user signs in as `alice-dev` with `Valid-password-123!` and follows the visible controls for the list and filter repository pull requests workflow. Seed values: pull requests `Improve onboarding` and `Fix search`, branches `main` and `feature-search`, reviewer `bob-reviewer`, check `test`."
    },
    {
     "keyword": "THEN",
     "content": "The page displays the required headings, controls, values, and status for the list and filter repository pull requests workflow. Seed values: pull requests `Improve onboarding` and `Fix search`, branches `main` and `feature-search`, reviewer `bob-reviewer`, check `test`."
    },
    {
     "keyword": "THEN",
     "content": "After refreshing or reopening the visible destination, the successful result remains persisted; a rejected action leaves the original state unchanged. Seed values: pull requests `Improve onboarding` and `Fix search`, branches `main` and `feature-search`, reviewer `bob-reviewer`, check `test`."
    }
   ]
  }
 ]
}
