{
 "id": "REQ-6-2-2",
 "name": "Compare Branches Before Opening a Pull Request",
 "type": "ATOMIC",
 "dependencies": [
  "REQ-4-3-1",
  "REQ-1-1-2"
 ],
 "description": "The PR comparison page is a read-only page shown before creation: base is the target branch that receives the merge result, and compare is the source branch that provides the changes to merge. A user with Write, Maintain, Admin, or organization Owner status clicks “New pull request” on the “Pull requests” page and selects the two branches; the system calculates comparable commits, changed files, and a diff summary based on the commits they currently point to. If the branches are the same or there is no difference, the creation entry is disabled; comparison does not save a PR, commit, or branch change. This feature builds on the persisted objects, opened pages, or authenticated-session context provided by REQ-4-3-1 (List and Switch Repository Branches) and REQ-1-1-2 (Sign In with an Existing Account); it must reuse that context and keep pages and data consistent after the context changes. Only signed-in users with Write, Maintain, Admin, or organization Owner status may compare branches on the repository pull-request page; Read and Triage may view existing PRs but cannot enter the creation-comparison flow. The system validates the role and rejects unauthorized requests. New pull request is a link. The comparison page has native select controls with combobox roles named base and compare; each option's visible label is its exact branch name. Compare changes is a button. For a valid selection it displays the known changed file path verbatim, a Commit summary with the comparable commit count, and an enabled Create pull request button. Selecting the same branch in both fields immediately displays No changes and disables the creation button, without requiring Compare changes to be clicked first. Clicking Compare changes retains that result. Seed data supplies a contributor with Write permission, a public repository PR-list page entry, a base branch, a distinct compare branch ahead by at least one commit, and a known changed file. Separate valid comparison page entrys open the same usable creation flow with the branches already selected; these pairs have no existing Open or Draft PR at the start of each creation scenario.\n\nThe seeded changed-file path for comparison is `src/search.ts`.\n\nScreenshot reference:\n![image](reference/github-compare-branches.png)",
 "scenarios": [
  {
   "name": "REQ-6-2-2: Compare Branches Before Opening a Pull Request - Scenario 1",
   "steps": [
    {
     "keyword": "GIVEN",
     "content": "The visitor starts at the application home page in a fresh unauthenticated browser session. The seeded data is pull requests `Improve onboarding` and `Fix search`, branches `main` and `feature-search`, reviewer `bob-reviewer`, check `test`. A signed-in user with Write, Maintain, Admin, or organization Owner status opens the “Pull requests” page; `feature-search` is one commit ahead of `main` and modifies one file. Seed values: pull requests `Improve onboarding` and `Fix search`, branches `main` and `feature-search`, reviewer `bob-reviewer`, check `test`."
    },
    {
     "keyword": "WHEN",
     "content": "The user clicks “New pull request”, selects `main` as base and `feature-search` as compare, and clicks “Compare changes”. Seed values: pull requests `Improve onboarding` and `Fix search`, branches `main` and `feature-search`, reviewer `bob-reviewer`, check `test`."
    },
    {
     "keyword": "THEN",
     "content": "The comparison page displays both branch names, at least one comparable commit, changed files, and a diff summary, and provides an enabled “Create pull request” entry. Seed values: pull requests `Improve onboarding` and `Fix search`, branches `main` and `feature-search`, reviewer `bob-reviewer`, check `test`."
    },
    {
     "keyword": "THEN",
     "content": "After changing compare to `main`, the page explains that the branches are the same or have no differences and disables the creation entry; this read-only comparison does not create a PR or modify branches. Seed values: pull requests `Improve onboarding` and `Fix search`, branches `main` and `feature-search`, reviewer `bob-reviewer`, check `test`."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "name": "REQ-6-2-2: Compare Branches Before Opening a Pull Request - Scenario 2",
   "steps": [
    {
     "keyword": "GIVEN",
     "content": "The visitor starts at the application home page in a fresh unauthenticated browser session. The seeded data is pull requests `Improve onboarding` and `Fix search`, branches `main` and `feature-search`, reviewer `bob-reviewer`, check `test`. A collaborator opens the comparison view on a page where base and compare branches can be selected. Seed values: pull requests `Improve onboarding` and `Fix search`, branches `main` and `feature-search`, reviewer `bob-reviewer`, check `test`."
    },
    {
     "keyword": "WHEN",
     "content": "The collaborator selects the same branch for both base and compare and clicks Compare changes. Seed values: pull requests `Improve onboarding` and `Fix search`, branches `main` and `feature-search`, reviewer `bob-reviewer`, check `test`."
    },
    {
     "keyword": "THEN",
     "content": "The system explains that the two branches are the same or have no differences and keeps the pull-request creation entry disabled. Seed values: pull requests `Improve onboarding` and `Fix search`, branches `main` and `feature-search`, reviewer `bob-reviewer`, check `test`."
    }
   ]
  }
 ]
}
