{
 "id": "REQ-6-2-3",
 "name": "Create a Pull Request from Comparison Results",
 "type": "ATOMIC",
 "dependencies": [
  "REQ-6-2-2"
 ],
 "description": "The valid comparison page is directly accessible to the signed-in contributor. Its Create pull request button opens a form with a field labeled Title, an optional Description field, and a single Create pull request submit button; the comparison-page action is no longer a competing active button. Successful submission shows the entered title as the exact PR heading and visible Open status, and the title survives reload. A title containing only spaces is rejected with Title is required and creates no PR. A user with Write, Maintain, or Admin clicks “Create pull request” on a valid comparison-results page, enters a title containing 1–256 non-empty characters after trimming leading and trailing whitespace and an optional description of at most 65536 characters, confirms distinct base/compare branches with differences, and clicks “Create pull request”. The system atomically creates an Open PR, stores a unique repository-scoped number, source/target branches, current compare commit, current base commit, title, description, author, creation time, and activity record, and redirects to the detail page; if there is no difference, the branches are the same, a Draft or Open PR with the same source/target pair already exists, the title is empty or overlong, the user lacks permission, or submission fails, no record is created. This feature builds on the persisted objects, opened pages, or authenticated-session context provided by REQ-6-2-2 (Compare Branches Before Opening a Pull Request); it must reuse that context and keep pages and data consistent after the context changes.",
 "scenarios": [
  {
   "name": "REQ-6-2-3: Create a Pull Request from Comparison Results - Scenario 1",
   "steps": [
    {
     "keyword": "GIVEN",
     "content": "The visitor starts at the application home page in a fresh unauthenticated browser session. The seeded data is pull requests `Improve onboarding` and `Fix search`, branches `main` and `feature-search`, reviewer `bob-reviewer`, check `test`. A signed-in collaborator is on a valid comparison-results page for `main` and `feature-search`; the page displays at least one changed file, and no open PR currently exists for that comparison. Seed values: pull requests `Improve onboarding` and `Fix search`, branches `main` and `feature-search`, reviewer `bob-reviewer`, check `test`."
    },
    {
     "keyword": "WHEN",
     "content": "The user clicks “Create pull request”, enters a title 1 to 256 characters long and an optional description, confirms base as `main` and compare as `feature-search`, and submits. Seed values: pull requests `Improve onboarding` and `Fix search`, branches `main` and `feature-search`, reviewer `bob-reviewer`, check `test`."
    },
    {
     "keyword": "THEN",
     "content": "The system redirects to the new PR detail page, which displays a unique repository-scoped number, Open status, source/target branches, title, description, and the current user as author. Seed values: pull requests `Improve onboarding` and `Fix search`, branches `main` and `feature-search`, reviewer `bob-reviewer`, check `test`."
    },
    {
     "keyword": "THEN",
     "content": "After refreshing the detail page and PR list, the PR still exists; if the title is blank or overlong, the branches are the same, there is no difference, the user lacks creation permission, or persistence fails, no partial record is created. Seed values: pull requests `Improve onboarding` and `Fix search`, branches `main` and `feature-search`, reviewer `bob-reviewer`, check `test`."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "name": "REQ-6-2-3: Create a Pull Request from Comparison Results - Scenario 2",
   "steps": [
    {
     "keyword": "GIVEN",
     "content": "The visitor starts at the application home page in a fresh unauthenticated browser session. The seeded data is pull requests `Improve onboarding` and `Fix search`, branches `main` and `feature-search`, reviewer `bob-reviewer`, check `test`. The visitor starts at the application home page in a fresh unauthenticated browser session. Seed values: pull requests `Improve onboarding` and `Fix search`, branches `main` and `feature-search`, reviewer `bob-reviewer`, check `test`."
    },
    {
     "keyword": "WHEN",
     "content": "The user signs in as `alice-dev` with `Valid-password-123!` and follows the visible controls for the create a pull request from comparison results workflow. Seed values: pull requests `Improve onboarding` and `Fix search`, branches `main` and `feature-search`, reviewer `bob-reviewer`, check `test`."
    },
    {
     "keyword": "THEN",
     "content": "The page displays the required headings, controls, values, and status for the create a pull request from comparison results workflow. Seed values: pull requests `Improve onboarding` and `Fix search`, branches `main` and `feature-search`, reviewer `bob-reviewer`, check `test`."
    },
    {
     "keyword": "THEN",
     "content": "After refreshing or reopening the visible destination, the successful result remains persisted; a rejected action leaves the original state unchanged. Seed values: pull requests `Improve onboarding` and `Fix search`, branches `main` and `feature-search`, reviewer `bob-reviewer`, check `test`."
    }
   ]
  }
 ]
}
