{
 "id": "REQ-6-2-4",
 "name": "Create a Draft Pull Request",
 "type": "ATOMIC",
 "dependencies": [
  "REQ-6-2-2"
 ],
 "description": "A visible draft comparison entry offers a Create draft pull request button, which opens the form containing Title and optional Description fields and one Create draft pull request submit button. Successful creation visibly shows Draft and a present but disabled Merge pull request button. A dedicated ready-for-review seed PR is separate from draft creation, belongs to the supplied author, initially has no submitted reviews, and displays its title, source branch, and target branch verbatim. Its Ready for review button changes the same PR to Open; if confirmation is used, it is a single Confirm button. Afterward the Draft status marker disappears, the title and branches are unchanged, and a Ready for review activity appears; Open persists on reload. A user with Write, Maintain, or Admin completes a valid base/compare branch selection, clicks “Create draft pull request”, enters a valid title and optional description, and confirms creation. The system creates a PR in Draft state using the same persisted fields as a normal PR and displays a “Draft” marker; a draft cannot submit reviews or be merged. Only the author, Maintain, Admin, or organization Owner may click “Ready for review” on a Draft detail page to convert it to Open and record an activity; this transition does not change branches, commits, title, or number. This feature builds on the persisted objects, opened pages, or authenticated-session context provided by REQ-6-2-2 (Compare Branches Before Opening a Pull Request); it must reuse that context and keep pages and data consistent after the context changes.",
 "scenarios": [
  {
   "name": "REQ-6-2-4: Create a Draft Pull Request - Scenario 1",
   "steps": [
    {
     "keyword": "GIVEN",
     "content": "The visitor starts at the application home page in a fresh unauthenticated browser session. The seeded data is pull requests `Improve onboarding` and `Fix search`, branches `main` and `feature-search`, reviewer `bob-reviewer`, check `test`. A signed-in collaborator is on a valid comparison page for two distinct branches with differences and has permission to create a PR. Seed values: pull requests `Improve onboarding` and `Fix search`, branches `main` and `feature-search`, reviewer `bob-reviewer`, check `test`."
    },
    {
     "keyword": "WHEN",
     "content": "The user clicks “Create draft pull request”, enters a valid title and optional description, and confirms creation. Seed values: pull requests `Improve onboarding` and `Fix search`, branches `main` and `feature-search`, reviewer `bob-reviewer`, check `test`."
    },
    {
     "keyword": "THEN",
     "content": "The system creates a detail page displaying the “Draft” marker and source/target branches, and the PR list also shows draft status; the “Merge pull request” entry cannot be executed. Seed values: pull requests `Improve onboarding` and `Fix search`, branches `main` and `feature-search`, reviewer `bob-reviewer`, check `test`."
    },
    {
     "keyword": "THEN",
     "content": "After refresh, the draft status and content remain; if there is no valid difference or creation fails, no draft record is created. Seed values: pull requests `Improve onboarding` and `Fix search`, branches `main` and `feature-search`, reviewer `bob-reviewer`, check `test`."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "name": "REQ-6-2-4: Create a Draft Pull Request - Scenario 2",
   "steps": [
    {
     "keyword": "GIVEN",
     "content": "The visitor starts at the application home page in a fresh unauthenticated browser session. The seeded data is pull requests `Improve onboarding` and `Fix search`, branches `main` and `feature-search`, reviewer `bob-reviewer`, check `test`. The PR author is signed in and has opened the detail page of a Draft PR they created titled `Draft onboarding update`, using source branch `draft-feature` and target branch `main`; the page displays the “Ready for review” button and no review has yet been submitted. Seed values: pull requests `Improve onboarding` and `Fix search`, branches `main` and `feature-search`, reviewer `bob-reviewer`, check `test`."
    },
    {
     "keyword": "WHEN",
     "content": "The author clicks “Ready for review” and confirms. Seed values: pull requests `Improve onboarding` and `Fix search`, branches `main` and `feature-search`, reviewer `bob-reviewer`, check `test`."
    },
    {
     "keyword": "THEN",
     "content": "The system saves the same PR number's status from Draft to Open, removes the Draft badge, and appends a status event in Conversation; after refresh and after reopening by a reviewer, the PR is shown as Open. This operation does not change the PR's branches, commits, title, or description. Seed values: pull requests `Improve onboarding` and `Fix search`, branches `main` and `feature-search`, reviewer `bob-reviewer`, check `test`."
    }
   ]
  }
 ]
}
